// ControlService — the unary control plane.
//
// Every RPC here is one request, one settled answer: the server
// marshals the call onto the app's UI goroutine, waits for the settle
// barrier (the frame the call's Sets asked for has been composed), and
// only then answers. Reading the screen immediately after invoking a
// command therefore sees the new pixels — the same guarantee the MCP
// bridge gives today, promoted to the contract.
//
// Errors are gRPC status codes, not payload fields:
//   NOT_FOUND            — no such name in the binding context / tree
//   INVALID_ARGUMENT     — type mismatch (message names both types),
//                          bad markup, bad gesture, bad registration
//   FAILED_PRECONDITION  — no markup context, no live composition
//   DEADLINE_EXCEEDED    — the UI goroutine did not answer in time
//                          (the run loop is blocked or not running)

